heories, current issues, and design philosophies. \n16. Demonstrate knowledge of the following subject areas: Interior Design; Interior Construction and utilities; Color Theory; Furniture Design and Construction; History of Arts and Interior Design; Materials of Design and Decoration and Professional Practice and Ethics\n17. Effectively function and assimilate within a collaborative framework in multi-disciplinary teams and task forces.\n18. Convey and communicate effectively through visual, oral, written and virtual communication, whether interpersonally, through the mass media, or through electronic means or advanced ICT Technologies.\n19. Understand, apply, and practice ethical professional values and responsibility.  \n20. Exhibit sensitivity through cultural, social and environmental issues and advocacies.  \n21. Design and conduct surveys, interviews, analyze and interpret data to meet desired needs of clients in interior design projects.\n22. Recognize the need to engage through lifelong learning.', 806, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-30 00:23:12', '2026-06-30 00:23:12'),
